This directory is intentionally empty.

Vercel runs `npm run build` (nest build) and then looks for a static output
directory, failing the deploy with:

    No Output Directory named "public" found after the Build completed.

There is no static site here — every request is served by the serverless
function in `api/index.ts`, and `vercel.json` rewrites `/(.*)` to it, so
nothing is ever served from this directory. It exists only to satisfy that
check.

Not solved by pointing outputDirectory at `dist/`: that is compiled server
code, and naming it as the static root invites it being served.
